-- The rows of WideWorldImporters which the persisters refer a new row to, and which the in-memory H2 database
-- of the -test unit, generated empty, would not have: Person_Persister makes a new person last edited by the
-- installed person 1, and Customer_Persister bills a new customer to the installed customer 1. Each is copied
-- from the database as it is, with the rows it refers to, but for its computed columns, which H2 computes not;
-- generated from the database, not to be edited by hand.
--
-- Person 1, Data Conversion Only, is last edited by itself, and customer 1 billed to itself: a single INSERT of
-- each satisfies its foreign key, as it does in SQL Server. The sequence of each table's key restarts past the
-- rows, so that the provider's keys do not take theirs.

